<!-- ======================================================== -->
<!-- SECTION 5: AUDIT & SOFT DELETE                           -->
<!-- ======================================================== -->
<h1>5. Common Audit Columns &amp; Enterprise Soft-Delete Mechanics</h1>
<p>
  A critical architectural requirement in enterprise ERP development is ensuring that data is never physically destroyed by default. Hard SQL deletes violate referential integrity, break relational foreign key constraints, and erase historical financial data required for legal audits.
</p>

<h2>5.1 The `AuditSoftDeleteMixin` Standard</h2>
<p>
  Every manageable business entity inherits from the global <code>AuditSoftDeleteMixin</code> located in <code>app/models/mixins.py</code>. This standardizes nine mandatory columns across the database:
</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 20%;">Column Name</th>
      <th style="width: 30%;">SQL Data Type &amp; Constraints</th>
      <th style="width: 50%;">Operational Purpose &amp; Behavior</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>id</code></td>
      <td><code>INTEGER</code>, Primary Key, Auto Increment</td>
      <td>Surrogate primary key guaranteeing unique identity for every record.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>created_at</code></td>
      <td><code>DATETIME</code>, Default UTC Now, Not Null</td>
      <td>Immutable UTC timestamp capturing the exact second the record was inserted.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>created_by</code></td>
      <td><code>INTEGER</code>, FK to <code>users.id</code>, Nullable</td>
      <td>Audit identifier of the authenticated user who initiated record creation.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>updated_at</code></td>
      <td><code>DATETIME</code>, Default UTC Now, Auto-Update</td>
      <td>Automatically refreshed UTC timestamp whenever record attributes change.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>updated_by</code></td>
      <td><code>INTEGER</code>, FK to <code>users.id</code>, Nullable</td>
      <td>Audit identifier of the authenticated user who modified the record.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>status</code></td>
      <td><code>VARCHAR(30)</code>, Default 'Active', Not Null</td>
      <td>Operational business state (e.g., Active, Suspended, Completed, Closed).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>is_deleted</code></td>
      <td><code>BOOLEAN</code>, Default False, Indexed</td>
      <td>Soft-delete indicator flag. Excludes deleted records from standard business queries.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>deleted_at</code></td>
      <td><code>DATETIME</code>, Nullable</td>
      <td>Timestamp capturing the moment the record was moved to the Recycle Bin.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>deleted_by</code></td>
      <td><code>INTEGER</code>, FK to <code>users.id</code>, Nullable</td>
      <td>Audit identifier of the authenticated user who soft-deleted the record.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>5.2 Soft Deletion Lifecycle &amp; Recycle Bin Operations</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Safe Deletion Trigger:</strong> When an administrator clicks "Delete" on any entity (e.g., employee, department, asset), the system invokes <code>record.soft_delete(user_id)</code>. This flags <code>is_deleted = True</code>, records the UTC timestamp, and stores the user's ID without physically executing a SQL <code>DELETE</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Query Isolation:</strong> Normal listings and dropdown selectors execute <code>Model.active_query()</code>, automatically filtering out records where <code>is_deleted == True</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Recycle Bin Oversight:</strong> Administrators can navigate to <code>/recycle-bin/</code> which executes <code>Model.trash_query()</code>, presenting soft-deleted items across departments, designations, projects, tasks, clients, and assets.</li>
  <li><strong>One-Click Restoration:</strong> Clicking "Restore" invokes <code>record.restore(user_id)</code>, which resets <code>is_deleted = False</code>, clears the deletion timestamps, and reinstates the entity into active system views.</li>
  <li><strong>Permanent Purge:</strong> Permanent physical removal from the database is restricted strictly to the Super Admin role for compliance with data privacy regulations.</li>
</ol>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<!-- ======================================================== -->
<!-- SECTION 6: MODULE WORKFLOWS                              -->
<!-- ======================================================== -->
<h1>6. Core Functional Modules &amp; Enterprise Workflows</h1>

<h2>6.1 Human Capital &amp; Employee Profile Management</h2>
<p>
  The Employee Management module manages the complete workforce lifecycle from recruitment to departure.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Workforce Directory:</strong> Filterable roster displaying employee codes, full names, job titles, departments, joining dates, and employment statuses.</li>
  <li><strong>Employee Code Generation:</strong> Automated formatting (e.g., <code>EMP-1001</code>) preventing duplicate employee identification numbers.</li>
  <li><strong>Comprehensive Profile View:</strong> Tabbed profile views displaying bio-data (DOB, blood group, nationality, passport), education degrees, prior employment history, skills matrix with proficiency levels, and emergency contacts.</li>
  <li><strong>Managerial Hierarchy:</strong> Supports self-referential reporting relationships, allowing department managers to oversee assigned subordinates.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.2 Biometric &amp; Virtual Attendance Tracking</h2>
<p>
  The Attendance module tracks employee presence and calculates working durations with automated validation.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Interactive Punch Terminal:</strong> Prominent dashboard banner enabling employees to Punch In (Check-In) and Punch Out (Check-Out) with real-time status indicators.</li>
  <li><strong>Working Hours Calculation:</strong> Automatically calculates decimal hours worked between arrival and departure timestamps.</li>
  <li><strong>Shift Management:</strong> Allows HR managers to configure work shifts with start/end times and grace periods.</li>
  <li><strong>Holiday Calendar:</strong> Integrates statutory and corporate holidays to ensure staff are not marked absent on official non-working days.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.3 Leave Management &amp; Managerial Approval Cycle</h2>
<p>
  The Leave module streamlines employee absence requests and balance tracking.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Entitlement Tracking:</strong> Manages quotas across Paid Annual, Sick, Casual, Maternity, and Unpaid leave types.</li>
  <li><strong>Application Submission:</strong> Employees submit leave applications with automatic day calculation and date validation.</li>
  <li><strong>Multi-Level Approval Workflow:</strong> Department Managers and HR evaluate pending requests, view reasons, and submit approval or rejection decisions with remarks.</li>
  <li><strong>Automated Quota Deduction:</strong> Upon approval, the system automatically deducts used days from the employee's active leave balance.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.4 Automated Monthly Payroll Engine &amp; Printable Salary Slips</h2>
<p>
  The Payroll module eliminates manual salary computation errors through automated batch processing.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Compensation Structure:</strong> Calculates basic wage, House Rent Allowance (HRA), medical allowances, and transport allowances.</li>
  <li><strong>Batch Generation Engine:</strong> Generates monthly payroll batches for all active personnel, factoring in approved bonuses and statutory withholdings.</li>
  <li><strong>Status Management:</strong> Batches progress from Draft review to official settlement (Mark as Paid).</li>
  <li><strong>Printable Salary Slip:</strong> Generates a formal, printable salary slip (<code>/payroll/payslip/&lt;id&gt;</code>) formatted with print CSS media queries for physical printing and digital PDF archival.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.5 Project Management &amp; Sprint Kanban Task Board</h2>
<p>
  The Project module facilitates collaborative task execution across departmental teams.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Project Deliverables:</strong> Tracks client contracts, project codes, target delivery dates, budgets, and milestones.</li>
  <li><strong>Sprint Kanban Board:</strong> Interactive 4-column visual board (<code>To-Do</code>, <code>In-Progress</code>, <code>Review</code>, <code>Completed</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Task Detail Modals:</strong> Allows assignees to update completion percentages, log estimated work hours, and participate in discussion threads.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.6 Client CRM &amp; Financial Invoicing / Expenses</h2>
<p>
  The Finance module manages client revenue receivables and corporate expense reimbursements.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Client CRM Directory:</strong> Maintains client business profiles, designated points of contact, and touchpoint interaction logs.</li>
  <li><strong>Invoicing Engine:</strong> Generates formal B2B client invoices with itemized totals, tax calculations, payment terms, and status tracking (<code>Sent</code>, <code>Partial</code>, <code>Paid</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Payment Recording:</strong> Records client payment receipts against outstanding invoice balances.</li>
  <li><strong>Expense Claims:</strong> Allows staff to submit corporate expense reimbursement claims with managerial review workflows.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.7 Physical Asset Inventory &amp; Custody Lifecycle</h2>
<p>
  The Asset module safeguards corporate equipment and tracks custody allocations.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Inventory Register:</strong> Tracks laptops, peripherals, mobile devices, and furniture with barcode asset tags and serial numbers.</li>
  <li><strong>Custody Assignment:</strong> Records hand-over dates, employee custodians, and equipment physical condition.</li>
  <li><strong>Equipment Return:</strong> Logs return dates and verifies equipment condition upon return to available inventory.</li>
  <li><strong>Staff Requisitions:</strong> Employees can submit requisitions for workstation equipment upgrades.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.8 Corporate Document Archiving &amp; Version Control</h2>
<p>
  The Document module provides a centralized repository for sensitive corporate files.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Document Taxonomy:</strong> Organizes files into categories (Policies, Legal, HR, Technical).</li>
  <li><strong>Automated Validation:</strong> Validates file uploads, detects extensions, and stores file sizes in KB/MB.</li>
  <li><strong>Version Tracking:</strong> Maintains revision history (e.g., v1.0, v1.1) preserving previous file versions and changelogs.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.9 Internal Communications &amp; Notice Board</h2>
<p>
  The Communication module keeps team members informed of organizational developments.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Company Notices:</strong> HR can publish priority announcements (Low, Medium, High, Urgent) with broadcast expiration dates.</li>
  <li><strong>Notification Feeds:</strong> Delivers personal real-time alerts with read/unread markers and target URL links.</li>
  <li><strong>Direct Messages:</strong> Internal peer-to-peer messaging system between registered system users.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.10 Global System Configuration &amp; Immutable Audit Trail</h2>
<p>
  The System module provides enterprise governance and compliance oversight.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>System Settings:</strong> Configures company name, corporate email, office hours, and default timezone.</li>
  <li><strong>User Account Oversight:</strong> Super Admin can manage user credentials, activate/deactivate accounts, and assign RBAC roles.</li>
  <li><strong>Immutable Audit Trail:</strong> Logs every database transaction with actor ID, table name, record ID, IP address, and JSON before/after snapshots.</li>
</ul>

<div class="page-break"></div>

