<!-- ======================================================== -->
<!-- SECTION 8: SECURITY & VALIDATION                         -->
<!-- ======================================================== -->
<h1>8. Security, Data Sanitization &amp; Form Validation</h1>
<p>
  The Office Management System enforces enterprise security standards based on OWASP Top 10 recommendations:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Cryptographic Password Hashing:</strong> Passwords are never stored in clear-text. Uses Werkzeug's salted <code>PBKDF2:SHA256</code> key derivation with 260,000 hashing rounds.</li>
  <li><strong>Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) Tokens:</strong> Every POST form embeds a cryptographically unique CSRF token validated via Flask-WTF before processing.</li>
  <li><strong>SQL Injection Immunity:</strong> All database queries are executed via SQLAlchemy parameterized object mapping. Raw user inputs are never concatenated into SQL strings.</li>
  <li><strong>Post-Redirect-Get (PRG) Pattern:</strong> Form submissions that modify state redirect to a GET endpoint upon success, preventing duplicate submissions if users refresh their browser.</li>
  <li><strong>Server-Side Form Validation:</strong> WTForms validates email syntax, integer/decimal ranges, non-empty fields, date order (end date &gt;= start date), and foreign key existence.</li>
  <li><strong>File Upload Security:</strong> Documents are stripped of directory traversal characters via <code>secure_filename()</code>, validated against permitted extensions, and saved outside the web root.</li>
</ul>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<!-- ======================================================== -->
<!-- SECTION 9: INSTALLATION & SETUP GUIDE                    -->
<!-- ======================================================== -->
<h1>9. Installation, Local Setup &amp; Database Seeding Guide</h1>
<p>
  Follow these steps to deploy and execute the OMS application on any Windows, macOS, or Linux development workstation:
</p>

<h2>Step 1: Environment Setup</h2>
<div class="code-snippet">
# Navigate to the project directory
cd d:\sites\office_management_system

# Create a Python virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate the virtual environment (Windows PowerShell)
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# Install production dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
</div>

<h2>Step 2: Database Initialization</h2>
<p>
  Ensure MySQL 8.0 or MariaDB is running on <code>localhost:3306</code>. Create the database:
</p>
<div class="code-snippet">
CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS oms_db CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
</div>
<p>Verify that your <code>.env</code> file contains the proper database URI:</p>
<div class="code-snippet">
SECRET_KEY=oms-super-secret-key-enterprise-2026
DATABASE_URL=mysql+pymysql://root:@localhost:3306/oms_db?charset=utf8mb4
FLASK_ENV=development
FLASK_APP=run.py
</div>

<h2>Step 3: Database Construction &amp; Seeding</h2>
<p>
  Run the automated seeder script to build all 68 relational tables and populate demo data:
</p>
<div class="code-snippet">
python seed.py
</div>
<p>
  <em>Verification: The script builds all 68 tables, seeds 4 RBAC roles, 4 user accounts, departments, designations, profiles, attendance records, leaves, payroll batches, sprint tasks, client invoices, and hardware assets.</em>
</p>

<h2>Step 4: Launching the Application</h2>
<div class="code-snippet">
python run.py
</div>
<p>
  Open your browser and navigate to: <strong><code>http://127.0.0.1:5000/auth/login</code></strong>
</p>

