<!-- SECTION 12: CONCLUSION                                   -->
<!-- ======================================================== -->
<h1>12. Conclusion &amp; Future Scope</h1>
<p>
  The <strong>Office Management System (OMS)</strong> successfully delivers a comprehensive, production-grade enterprise web solution that fulfills all academic and industry requirements. With <strong>68 normalized relational tables</strong>, four-tier Role-Based Access Control, automated payroll processing, an interactive Sprint Kanban board, virtual biometric attendance tracking, physical asset management, and a 47-report Business Intelligence hub, the system demonstrates the practical implementation of enterprise software engineering principles.
</p>

<h2>Future Roadmap</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Mobile Native Clients:</strong> Develop Flutter or React Native mobile applications consuming RESTful Flask API endpoints.</li>
  <li><strong>Physical Biometric Hardware Integration:</strong> Direct MQTT/TCP hardware integration with ZKTeco or Anviz biometric fingerprint and facial recognition attendance terminals.</li>
  <li><strong>Single Sign-On (SSO):</strong> Integration with enterprise identity providers via OAuth2, OpenID Connect, and SAML 2.0 (Google Workspace, Microsoft Entra ID).</li>
  <li><strong>Automated Email Notifications:</strong> Celery and Redis asynchronous task queues for automated dispatch of monthly salary slips, leave status notifications, and invoice payment reminders.</li>
</ul>

